  "generated_text": "To evaluate \\(\\log_3 27\\sqrt{3}\\), we start by expressing \\(27\\sqrt{3}\\) in terms of powers of 3.\n\nFirst, note that \\(27 = 3^3\\) and \\(\\sqrt{3} = 3^{1/2}\\). Therefore, we can rewrite \\(27\\sqrt{3}\\) as:\n\\[\n27\\sqrt{3} = 3^3 \\cdot 3^{1/2} = 3^{3 + 1/2} = 3^{7/2}\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to find \\(\\log_3 3^{7/2}\\). Using the property of logarithms that \\(\\log_b (a^c) = c \\log_b a\\), we get:\n\\[\n\\log_3 3^{7/2} = \\frac{7}{2} \\log_3 3 = \\frac{7}{2} \\cdot 1 = \\frac{7}{2}\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(\\log_3 27\\sqrt{3}\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{7}{2}}\n\\]",
